eaks that chow).  \n\nLet's check if we keep T2,T3,T4 chow and aim for W4,W5,W6 chow:  \nNeed W6. W6 has 4 left, good chance.  \n\nIf we keep W4,W5, discard W7,W8,T8 first.  \n\nWhich is most useless?  \nT8: no nearby tiles (T6 2 left, T7 1 left, T9 1 left), T7 already used a lot (next player has T7 pung). So T8 is dead.  \nW7,W8: only W9 needed for chow, only 1 W9 left, so unlikely.  \n\nSo discard among W7, W8, T8.  \n\nAlso consider safety:  \nOpponents\u2019 discards:  \nPrevious player discarded W7, W8 already (in history), so W7 or W8 might be relatively safe.  \nT8 was discarded by next player earlier, so also safe.  \n\nBut from tile count:  \nT8 (2 initially - 1 in hand - 1 discarded earlier = 0 left? Wait: T8 total 4, unshown now: 2 (per given count at start), so maybe safe.  \n\nHowever, improving hand shape:  \nIf we keep T2,T3,T4 chow, discard W8 (makes W7 useless but we can discard W7 next).  \n\nI think discard W8 first: it\u2019s a terminal in that sequence but not needed.  \n\n**Evaluation:**  \nPromising moves: Play W8 (useless now), Play T8 (useless), Play W7 (useless).  \nKeeping W4,W5 for W6 chance, keeping T2,T3,T4 chow, keeping B6 pair.  \n\n**Final choice:** Discard W8, then next discard W7, then see if draw helps.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nW8 is hardest to use given W9 scarcity; W7 similar but W8 first to keep W7 maybe for pairing if draw W7? We have no other W7 in hand, and W7 only 1 left in wall, so pairing W7 unlikely. So W8 slightly worse than W7 because W7 can still combine with W6,W8? No, W6,W7,W8 chow needs W6,W8 but W8 gone.  \nActually W7 can combine with W5,W6 chow? No. So both useless. But W8 is more terminal so slightly worse wait for others? But opponents have W7-W9 chow already, so maybe safe.\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation:** W8 is the weakest tile given remaining tiles and opponents\u2019 exposures.  \n**Reason:** With only one W9 left, the W7,W8,W9 chow is improbable, and W8 has no other chow possibilities. Keeping W4,W5 offers a better potential chow with W6 (4 left).  \n**Answer:** Play W8"}
